Use cWebLabel.pkg

/*
    Class:      cFTWebLabel
    Purpose:    A cWebLabel wearing this app's palette and text size, so a dialog does not have to
                dress one every time it places a caption.

                Created 2026-08-22. There was exactly ONE raw cWebLabel in the program - the note at
                the top of Target DataFlex Version - which is why this class did not exist while the
                other four FT control classes did. Nils asked for it once the FtCompact class landed:
                a per-control psCSSClass line is the kind of thing that gets copied to four dialogs
                and forgotten in the fifth.

                Carries no colours of its own. FtCompact styles the label, the field box and the
                value together in application.css, so a label and the field under it read as one
                control rather than two shades of near-white. The framework's psTextColor and
                friends are INLINE styles that no stylesheet can override - see the FtCompact note
                in application.css for why nothing here sets them.
*/

// Inherited from cWebLabel; stated so the Designer models this class without the pooled package.
{ DesignerJSClass=df.WebLabel }
Class cFTWebLabel is a cWebLabel

    Procedure Construct_Object
        Forward Send Construct_Object

        // The app's text size, not the framework's larger default - see FtCompact in application.css.
        Set psCSSClass to "FtCompact"
    End_Procedure

End_Class
